.TH GIT-VOUCH 1 "" "git-vouch" "git-vouch Manual"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
git-vouch \- check a kernel identity registry and export git's allowed-signers files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit vouch\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
\fBgit vouch\fR \fIcommand\fR \fB\-h\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
git-vouch answers whether a signer is a real person whom real people vouch for, and whether their key may sign here. People, endorsements and tier grants are signed files in a registry git repository; git vouch checks the registry's rules and writes the allowed_signers and revocation files that git's SSH signing reads. After \fBgit vouch setup\fR, plain \fBgit verify-tag\fR and \fBgit log \-\-show-signature\fR verify against the registry.
.PP
All signing and verification is done by \fBssh-keygen\fR(1) and \fBgit\fR(1); git-vouch contains no cryptography and uses only the Python standard library.
.PP
Commands that write records (\fBregister\fR, \fBadd-key\fR, \fBretire-key\fR, \fBendorse\fR, \fBapprove\fR, \fBrevoke\fR, \fBcosign\fR) work in the registry checkout in the current directory and never push: commit the files and send a branch for the registry maintainer to merge.
.PP
\fBgit vouch \-h\fR lists the commands, and \fBgit vouch\fR \fIcommand\fR \fB\-h\fR prints one command's help, which is what this page is made from.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS setup
\fBgit vouch setup\fR [\fB\-\-registry\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-tier\fR \fI{anchor,maintainer,contributor}\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-automation\fR | \fB\-\-no\-include\-automation\fR]
.PP
record the registry URL, configure git for SSH signing, and sync
.TP
\fB\-\-registry\fR \fIURL\fR
registry repository URL (default: the one configured, else the kernel's)
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-tier\fR \fI{anchor,maintainer,contributor}\fR
lowest tier exported, saved for later syncs (default: contributor)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-automation\fR | \fB\-\-no\-include\-automation\fR
also export automation keys, with namespaces="file"; saved
.SS sync
\fBgit vouch sync\fR [\fB\-\-min\-tier\fR \fI{anchor,maintainer,contributor}\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-automation\fR | \fB\-\-no\-include\-automation\fR]
.PP
fetch the registry without allowing a rewind, check it, and re-export
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-tier\fR \fI{anchor,maintainer,contributor}\fR
lowest tier exported, saved for later syncs (default: contributor)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-automation\fR | \fB\-\-no\-include\-automation\fR
also export automation keys, with namespaces="file"; saved
.SS status
\fBgit vouch status\fR
.PP
show the registry commit, its fetch age, and your own tier
.SS register
\fBgit vouch register\fR [\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fIPUBKEY\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-handle\fR \fIHANDLE\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-email\fR \fIEMAIL\fR] [\fB\-\-accountable\fR \fIHANDLE\fR] [\fB\-\-attestation\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-challenge\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.PP
write your person file and sign it in the registry checkout in the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR
private key file, or .pub to sign through the agent (default: git config user.signingKey)
.TP
\fIPUBKEY\fR
your .pub file
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fIFILE\fR
complete this draft
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fIEMAIL\fR
repeat for more addresses
.TP
\fB\-\-accountable\fR \fIHANDLE\fR
automation: your maintainer
.TP
\fB\-\-attestation\fR \fIFILE\fR
ssh-keygen -O write-attestation output
.TP
\fB\-\-challenge\fR \fIFILE\fR
the -O challenge file it was made with
.SS add\-key
\fBgit vouch add\-key\fR [\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR] \fIPUBKEY\fR [\fB\-\-attestation\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-challenge\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.PP
add a key to your person file and re-sign it in the registry checkout in the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR
private key file, or .pub to sign through the agent (default: git config user.signingKey)
.TP
\fIPUBKEY\fR
the new key's .pub file
.TP
\fB\-\-attestation\fR \fIFILE\fR
ssh-keygen -O write-attestation output
.TP
\fB\-\-challenge\fR \fIFILE\fR
the -O challenge file it was made with
.SS retire\-key
\fBgit vouch retire\-key\fR [\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR] \fIKEY\fR
.PP
retire a key in your person file and re-sign it in the registry checkout in the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR
private key file, or .pub to sign through the agent (default: git config user.signingKey)
.TP
\fIKEY\fR
\&.pub file, key text or did:key
.SS endorse
\fBgit vouch endorse\fR [\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fIhandle\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-email\fR \fIEMAIL\fR] [\fB\-\-note\fR \fINOTE\fR]
.PP
write and sign an endorsement in the registry checkout in the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR
private key file, or .pub to sign through the agent (default: git config user.signingKey)
.TP
\fIhandle\fR
whose current key, name and emails to endorse, as the checkout has them: check out the merged registry, not a pull request
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fIFILE\fR
sign this draft, such as one from git-vouch-migrate drafts
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fIEMAIL\fR
endorse only this address (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fINOTE\fR
how you know them
.SS approve
\fBgit vouch approve\fR [\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR] \fIhandle\fR \fI{maintainer,contributor,automation}\fR
.PP
write and sign a tier record in the registry checkout in the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR
private key file, or .pub to sign through the agent (default: git config user.signingKey)
.SS cosign
\fBgit vouch cosign\fR [\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR] \fIPATH\fR
.PP
as an anchor, approve the exact bytes of anchors.json or a person file in the registry checkout in the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR
private key file, or .pub to sign through the agent (default: git config user.signingKey)
.TP
\fIPATH\fR
anchors.json or people/<handle>.json
.SS revoke
\fBgit vouch revoke\fR [\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR] \fIKEY\fR [\fB\-\-subject\fR \fIHANDLE\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIREASON\fR]
.PP
write and sign a revocation in the registry checkout in the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-with\fR \fIFILE\fR
private key file, or .pub to sign through the agent (default: git config user.signingKey)
.TP
\fIKEY\fR
\&.pub file, key text or did:key
.TP
\fB\-\-subject\fR \fIHANDLE\fR
whose key, if two files list it
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIREASON\fR
default: compromise
.SS check
\fBgit vouch check\fR [\fIDIR\fR]
.PP
validate every signature and compute every tier
.TP
\fIDIR\fR
registry checkout (default: the synced copy once setup has run, else the current directory; pass . to check a checkout)
.SS export
\fBgit vouch export\fR [\fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-tier\fR \fI{anchor,maintainer,contributor}\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-automation\fR] [\fB\-\-allowed\-signers\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-revocation\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.PP
write the allowed-signers file and the revocation file
.TP
\fIDIR\fR
registry checkout (default: the synced copy once setup has run, else the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-tier\fR \fI{anchor,maintainer,contributor}\fR
lowest tier exported (default: contributor)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-automation\fR
also export automation keys, with namespaces="file"
.TP
\fB\-\-allowed\-signers\fR \fIFILE\fR
output file (default: git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile)
.TP
\fB\-\-revocation\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
output file (default: git config gpg.ssh.revocationFile)
.SS did
\fBgit vouch did\fR \fI<.pub file | ssh\-pubkey | did:key>\fR
.PP
print the did:key for an SSH public key, or the reverse
.SS query
\fBgit vouch query\fR (\fI<did:key>\fR | \fB\-\-all\fR) [\fB\-\-at\fR \fITIME\fR]
.PP
print a did:key's holder, tier and validity as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
print every listed did:key's answer as one JSON object
.TP
\fB\-\-at\fR \fITIME\fR
RFC 3339 time to answer for (default: now)
.SS keys
\fBgit vouch keys\fR \fI<email>\fR
.PP
print an endorsed email's current keys with their patatt selectors
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
\fBvouch.registry\fR
The registry URL; set by \fBsetup\fR.
.TP
\fBvouch.minTier, vouch.includeAutomation\fR
Export choices saved by \fBsetup\fR and \fBsync\fR.
.TP
\fBgpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile, gpg.ssh.revocationFile, gpg.format\fR
Set globally by \fBsetup\fR, only after its first sync succeeds, and never over a different existing value.
.TP
\fBuser.signingKey\fR
The default key for the signing commands; \fB\-\-sign-with\fR overrides it.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/git\-vouch/, else ~/.local/share/git\-vouch/\fR
The synced registry copy in \fIregistry/\fR, and the \fIallowed_signers\fR and \fIrevoked_keys\fR files git verifies against.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. 1 on any error: for \fBcheck\fR, any problem in the registry (warnings and void records alone exit 0); for \fBquery\fR and \fBkeys\fR, an unknown key or email.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-verify-tag\fR(1), \fBgit-config\fR(1), \fBssh-keygen\fR(1), \fBgit-vouch-migrate\fR(1).
.PP
README.md, DESIGN.md and docs/ in the git-vouch repository: https://github.com/MarkAtwood/git-vouch
